# JC3-Batmobile - never commit game files, extracted assets, or other people's software.
# Only our own code, notes, configs and build scripts belong in this repo.
#
# Verified with:  git status --porcelain -uall | Measure-Object -Line
# Anything listed there that is not ours is a hole in this file.

# --- Avalanche / JC3 engine formats -----------------------------------------
# These are extension patterns rather than path rules so that a stray copy dropped
# anywhere in the tree is still caught, not just one inside a known folder.
*.ee
# entity container table of contents, shipped beside the .ee
*.ee.toc
*.epe
*.rbm
*.lod
*.vmodc
*.physicsc
*.wtunec
*.cmtunec
*.ftunec
*.etunec
*.pfxc
*.efcc
*.bikc
*.fraglib
*.frag
*.stringlookup
*.fmod_guids
*.ddsc
*.hmddsc
*.adf
*.rtpc
*.pskx
*.psk
# Bink video, JC3 and most other Source-derived engines
*.btc
# animation container
*.ban
# animation state machine (aaf/animations)
*.asb
# animation state machine body
*.afsmb
# skeleton (aaf/animations/jc_skeletons)
*.bsk
# extracted texture trim data
*.trim
*.wem
*.atlas
*.filelist
@files.xml
*.filelist.txt
_filelist.txt

# --- meshes and textures extracted from the game -----------------------------
*.tga
*.dds
*.ddsx
*.obj
*.fbx
*.abc

# .max / .maxcompound are deliberately NOT ignored here. The 3ds Max install tree is
# covered by its own directory rule below, and the planned ApexMax/HavokMax round-trip
# workflow will want its scene files version-controlled. Any .max that is really a
# byproduct of the game goes in Working/ or Builds/, which are ignored by path.

# --- installed software and installers ---------------------------------------
# The 3ds Max tree is ~11 GB across ~71,000 files and the service packs another
# 3.8 GB. Neither belongs in a mod repo. Better still: move them off this disk's
# project folder entirely (e.g. C:\Tools\3dsMax2017) and delete these lines.
Autodesk 3ds Max/
Autodesk 3ds Max*/
*.iso
*.msi
*.exe
*.msp
*.cab

